plug-discard-file-blocks

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: On a guest restored from a snapshot memory file (MAP_PRIVATE), a newly plugged virtio-mem block is still mapped from that file, so the first write to each page reads the file into the page cache and copies it, charging the page cache to the guest cgroup, and the guest reads whatever the file holds there. The plug path now discards the newly plugged blocks of a private file mapping, mapping anonymous memory over them, and discard_range re-applies the region madvise advice so THP restores keep MADV_HUGEPAGE. Adds the plug_discard_fails metric.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream Firecracker maps newly plugged virtio-mem blocks of a file-restored guest anonymously, keeping the region madvise advice.
